dy-to-eat products, and prepared foods to retail and foodservice customers. This segment markets its packaged meat products under the Smithfield, Eckrich, Nathan's Famous, Farmland, Armour, Farmer John, Kretschmar, Krakus, John Morrell, Cook's, Gwaltney, Carando, Margherita, Curly's and Smithfield Culinary, as well as under private labels. The Fresh Pork segment processes live hogs into a variety of primal, sub-primal, and offal products, such as bellies, butts, hams, loins, trimmings, picnics, and ribs. This segment sells its fresh pork products to retail, foodservice and industrial customers, as well as to export markets, including China, Mexico, Japan, South Korea, and Canada. The Hog Production segment produces and raises its hogs on various company-owned farms and farms that are owned and operated by contract farmers. This segment also sells livestock feed and grains; and provides transportation and other ancillary services. The Other segment engages in the bioscience operations uses raw materials from hogs that process to manufacture heparin products, including an active pharmaceutical ingredient that mitigates the risk of blood clots; and produces fresh pork products in Mexico. The company was founded in 1936 and is headquartered in Smithfield, Virginia. Smithfield Foods, Inc. is a subsidiary of SFDS UK Holdings Limited.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Charles Shane Smith | President, CEO & Director | Age 51 | Compensation: $9.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 33K people. Revenue per employee of $464K ranks in the below the sector median among Consumer Defensive peers. Each employee generates $21K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $269 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 21\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Smithfield Foods, Inc. is a mid-cap consumer defensive business with a $7.6B market cap on $15.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +1% over the past three years and +1% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 11% against a 7% cost of capital, a 4-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, and 12% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $718M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.07\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 32\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 2.1% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 88% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.03446682550923594},{"text":"Elevated short interest (12.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $4.4M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-4398737.94},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Consumer Defensive peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Slow-motion taste and channel shifts \u2014 private label, Gen-Z health preferences, or a DTC disruption can erode decade-old brand moats without a single dramatic quarter.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Input cost inflation from agricultural commodities \u2014 when raw materials spike, pass-through pricing lags and margin compression is immediate.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 and health-trend demand destruction \u2014 weight-loss drugs and wellness shifts are structurally reducing consumption in snack, beverage, and packaged food categories.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 10% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 42% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Consumer Defensive sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 10% over 3 months","Consumer Defensive ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Better Dividend Stock for Retirees: Hormel vs. Smithfield Foods","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/better-dividend-stock-retirees-hormel-142901774.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794580141.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.44,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Friday Night Flights 2026: Nov. 13 Full Show","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/friday-night-flights-2026-nov-001822000.html","date":"2026-11-14","timestamp":1794620489.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.34,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Root Inc. Officer Jonathan A. Allison Files Form 144 to Sell 2,962 Class A Shares Worth $129K","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/root-inc-officer-jonathan-a-allison-files-form-144-to-sell-2962-class-a-shares-worth-129k","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794582926.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.477,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Tenable's Mark C. Thurmond Files Form 144 to Sell 7,830 Shares Under Rule 144","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/tenables-mark-c-thurmond-files-form-144